WEBVTT

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:09.160
A busy front desk never stops, even when nobody can answer the phone.

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:13.540
A client calls while the whole team is busy, and nobody picks up.

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:16.280
That caller doesn't leave a voicemail.

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:18.640
They call the next business on the list.

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:21.600
Every missed call is a booked appointment you never see.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:27.080
And after hours calls, when people finally have time to call, are guaranteed losses.

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:31.520
A full-time receptionist costs more than the business earns after dark.

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:33.480
The gap isn't your service.

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:37.000
Worry not, I'm here to close your loop.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:39.480
Here's what happens now, automatically.

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:42.440
The AI receptionist answers the phone.

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:45.960
It sounds like a person, and it talks like a person.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:48.920
But the real work starts the second the call ends.

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:51.000
First, it remembers who called.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:55.720
Every call is written down, so nothing gets processed twice.

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:59.160
You never get a double booking, because of a system hiccup.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:02.440
Then it decides, can this caller actually be booked?

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:08.360
If they asked a question or picked a date that doesn't exist, it gets noted and filed.

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:10.840
Nothing breaks, nothing is lost.

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:12.840
Then it looks at your real calendar.

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:17.080
If the slot they want is open, the appointment goes straight in.

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:21.000
Service, staff member, and the client's number all set for you.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:25.160
If the slot is already taken, it doesn't just drop them.

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:29.960
The call is marked and saved, so you can call them back today instead of losing them.

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:37.160
And every single call, booked, not booked, or needs a call back, ends up on one sheet you can

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:41.960
open anytime, plus a short email to you when something needs your attention.

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:43.480
You never touch a spreadsheet.

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:45.960
You never listen to a voicemail.

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:48.280
You just show up for the appointments.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:53.880
If you're a clinic, there's a version built for healthcare privacy rules too.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:58.040
Your next missed call answers itself, bring your services, and your hours.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:01.400
And I'll show you the calls you're losing today.

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:04.040
I'm Christian, NEDN Automation Architect.

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:06.040
Book a discovery call now.
